  "notes": "All figures copied as published. Texas Medicaid/CHIP limits are monthly MAGI household income limits from Texas Works Handbook C-131.1 (Rev. 26-2, eff. Apr 1 2026). Code-to-group mapping: TWH glossary and A-820 (TP 43 under 1, TP 48 ages 1-5, TP 44 ages 6-18, TP 40 pregnant women), C-131.1 header (TA 84 = CHIP, TA 85 = CHIP-P), W-1410 (TA 41 = HTW income limit). The 198% column also covers TP 42, TP 35, TP 36, TA 74; 133% also TP 34, TA 76; 144% also TP 33, TA 75 (emergency/other codes). TA 77 (400%) and TP 70 (413%) are recorded but their program names were not confirmed from an official source. C-131.4 separately lists a standard MAGI income disregard of 5 percentage points of FPL; C-131.1 does not state whether its limits already include it, so check TWH A-1341 before applying it. Parents/caretaker relatives (TP 08) limits are flat monthly dollar amounts (C-131.2, Rev. 15-4, eff. Oct 1 2015), not % FPL; size 1 two-parent is N/A. The school meals 2026-27 table is a graphic in the Federal Register; values were transcribed and all 80 cross-checked against the notice's stated formula (2026 FPL x 1.30 / 1.85 rounded up; monthly = annual/12, twice-monthly /24, bi-weekly /26, weekly /52, rounded up). WIC (185%) equals the reduced-price meal limit. fns.usda.gov returned HTTP 403, so Federal Register notices were used. Alaska/Hawaii omitted. School meals 2025-26 not included.",
  "verified_date": "2026-09-26",
  "verification_notes": "Independently re-verified 2026-09-26 against official sources. (1) Texas Works Handbook C-131 page (fhb.hhs.texas.gov): all C-131.1 values (133/144/198/201/202/204.2/400/413% columns, sizes 1-8 and each additional), column codes, the March 1, 2026 column date, Rev. 26-2 eff. Apr 1 2026; C-131.2 (Rev. 15-4 eff. Oct 1 2015) all three columns incl. N/A for size-1 two-parent; C-131.3 (TP 07, 185%) and C-131.4 (5% FPL disregard) all match exactly. A-820 confirms age ranges for TP 43/48/44 (through last day of month of 1st/6th birthday; through month they turn 19); W-1410 confirms HTW uses TA 41 income limit. (2) WIC 2026-27 and 2025-26 48-state tables re-read from Federal Register full text (91 FR 23050; 90 FR 11598): all 80 values plus additional-member rows match; notices confirm 2026 HHS poverty guidelines at 91 FR 1797 (Jan 15, 2026) and the 100% FPL column confirms the 2026 HHS guideline values (15,960 + 5,680 per person). (3) School meals 2026-27: official table image EN09AP26.001 read directly; all free (130%) and reduced (185%) 48-state values and additional-member rows match; also recomputed from stated formula (x1.30/x1.85, /12,/24,/26,/52, rounded up) with zero mismatches. Changes: removed unconfirmed CHIP ages field (\"under 19\") because the fetched C-131 page does not state CHIP ages; added FR page citations to sources. No numeric values needed correction. Still unconfirmed (retained as published, not interpreted): program names for TA 77 and TP 70; whether C-131.1 limits already include the 5% MAGI disregard."
